{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Trie"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Keys are sequences of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"text":" symbols, stored as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Symbol]"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Character>"},{"text":" holds words,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Unicode.Scalar>"},{"text":" the same words scalar by scalar, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<UInt8>"},{"text":" byte strings. Lookup,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"insertion and removal follow the key down from the root, O(","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"m","type":"text"}]},{"text":"·","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"σ","type":"text"}]},{"text":") for a key of ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"m","type":"text"}]},{"text":" symbols","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and at most ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"σ"}]},{"text":" children per vertex. A trie answers the queries a hash set cannot: every key","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with a prefix, whether any key has one, and the longest key that is a prefix of a query.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let words = Trie([\"car\", \"cart\", \"cat\", \"dog\"])","words.contains(\"cat\")                                   \/\/ true","words.elements(withPrefix: \"car\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ [\"car\", \"cart\"]","words.longestPrefix(of: \"carton\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ \"cart\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iteration visits each key before the keys it is a prefix of. When the symbols are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Comparable"},{"type":"text","text":", each vertex keeps its children sorted, so the keys come in lexicographic order;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"otherwise children come in the order they were first added."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertices live in flat arrays with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int32"},{"text":" links, so the trie holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices, and copying it copies a few arrays only when one copy is mutated.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tries\/trie"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree"],"anchor":"Sets-of-sequences","title":"Sets of sequences","generated":true}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie\/PrefixView"],"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie\/init()","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie\/init(_:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie\/count","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tr